      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial alloy is in an as-sintered state.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial alloy is microstructurally homogeneous.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A prior Hf-coated VZrHfNbTa material used an Hf coating approximately 120 μm thick.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf coating should improve oxidation resistance at approximately 1000°C in air for exposures up to 200 hours.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation of the Hf-coated alloy forms a dense HfO2 layer at the surface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting HfO2 layer is adherent.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, the Hf coating oxidizes preferentially to HfO2.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HfO2 scale is stable at the stated elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HfO2 scale grows slowly.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HfO2 scale has low oxygen permeability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dense HfO2 layer acts as a barrier that impedes oxygen ingress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HfO2 layer prevents excessive internal oxidation of the underlying alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf coating reduces degradation of the underlying refractory alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-coated alloy has lower oxidation weight gain per unit area than an uncoated control.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
